[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Open Games (1...e5)"]
[Variation "Scotch Game: Göring Gambit Declined"]
[ECO "C44"]
[Character "sharp,positional"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "counter-in-the-centre,give-back-material"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "gambit"]
[Opponent "3.d4 exd4 4.c3"]
[Start "scotch-game 3...exd4"]

4. c3 { White offers another pawn for a lead in development: the Göring Gambit. } 4... d5 { Do not take on c3. Hit back in the centre at once, so White's extra tempo has nothing to attack. } 5. exd5 Qxd5 { Takes back the pawn, and the queen is safe in the centre for now. } 6. cxd4 Bb4+ { A check first: White must block, and Black keeps control of d5. } 7. Nc3 { Blocks the check with a developing move, and the knight attacks the queen. } 7... Bg4 { Develops with a pin on the knight on f3, so White cannot use it freely. } 8. Be2 { Develops and prepares castling. It also gets out of the way of the pin on f3. } 8... Bxf3 { Takes the knight that guards d4. } 9. Bxf3 { Takes back with the bishop, which now eyes the black queen and knight. } 9... Qc4 { Moves the queen with a threat on c3 and the bishop. Black has an equal game; plan: ...Nge7, ...O-O-O and trade queens if White allows it. } *
